  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Color Mappings**\n\nI\'ve discovered numerous components employing `bg-white` without corresponding dark mode counterparts. They depend on `--color-white-var` to resolve to `#111827` in dark mode. Removing the color variable would have wide-reaching consequences.\n\n\n**Evaluating Dark Mode Strategy**\n\nI\'m now contemplating how to handle the dark mode implementation more systematically. The current approach is inconsistent; some components use `dark:` classes while others rely on CSS variable hacks. I\'m torn between two options: a comprehensive update across all relevant files to use `dark:` classes everywhere, or retaining the CSS variable hack in `index.css`. The first approach seems cleaner but more time-consuming, while the second could maintain the current style, with its downsides.\n\n\n**Refining Variable Definitions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how Tailwind v4 handles colors natively. I see that the existing setup redefines basic colors like `--color-white`, which seems counterintuitive. I\'m leaning towards using the `@theme` directive to map custom variables to standard color names. This should streamline dark mode and ensure consistent color handling, using variables like `--color-background` or `--color-surface`. I need to ensure that this approach is consistent with the latest updates of UX components.\n\n\n**Investigating Color Variables**\n\nI\'m now diving into the color variable situation. I noticed `index.css` defines `--color-primary-*` as blue, while `--color-orange-*` is custom. Tailwind v4 uses standard Oklch colors by default; `--color-orange-50` is pre-defined. Removing `@theme` definitions for gray and orange appears to use custom hex codes. However, removing `--color-gray-50: var(--gray-50)` from `@theme` would default to Tailwind\'s built-in gray, which is then redefined by `.dark`. It seems the project\'s Tailwind v3 config is outdated, and the use of `@tailwindcss/vite` suggests a more recent setup.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 543831233
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
