    thinking: "**Mapping Tailwind Colors**\n\nI\'ve realized that overriding `--color-*` within the `.dark` class effectively cascades down to all utility classes. This is fantastic! It implies I can streamline the `index.css` file by directly mapping Tailwind\'s standard colors within the `.dark` class, eliminating the need for those custom properties like `--bg-gray` or `--color-white-var`. I need to check if Tailwind v4 already has this capability.\n\n\n**Refining Dark Mode Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to best handle the color mapping for dark mode, specifically how to invert the grays and handle the white color. The goal is to avoid redundancy and streamline the code. Examining the existing `index.css`, I am exploring how to effectively map `--color-white` to `var(--color-gray-900)` in dark mode and invert the gray scale. A key goal is to see if standard Tailwind v4 CSS variables can be leveraged to simplify the implementation.\n\n\n**Resolving Circular Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag with the dark mode color mapping: circular dependencies. Assigning `--color-gray-50` to `--color-gray-900` within the `.dark` class leads to a recursive definition, overriding itself. I\'ve realized that redefining Tailwind\'s base color variables within `.dark` necessitates the use of literal hex codes or `oklch()` values. I will now examine these definitions, in isolation, to verify how the colors will render.\n\n\n"
